22:21:38  CALL    send_email({'body': 'Hello,\n\nBelow is a concise summary of key information on Artificial Intelligence (AI) based on recent research:\n\n**Definition**\n- AI is the field of computer science focused on creating systems that perform tasks requiring human intelligence (perception, reasoning, learning, decision‑making).\n\n**Historical Milestones**\n- 1950: Alan Turing’s Turing Test.\n- 1956: Dartmouth Workshop coins “Artificial Intelligence.”\n- 1970s‑80s: Expert systems (e.g., MYCIN).\n- 1997: IBM Deep\u202fBlue defeats world chess champion.\n- 2012: AlexNet’s breakthrough in deep learning (ImageNet).\n- 2018‑2023: Large language models (GPT‑3, GPT‑4, PaLM, LLaMA) reach human‑level language generation.\n\n**Core Sub‑fields**\n- Machine Learning (ML) – algorithms that improve from data.\n- Deep Learning – multi‑layer neural networks.\n- Natural Language Processing (NLP).\n- Computer Vision.\n- Robotics.\n- Knowledge Representation & Reasoning.\n- AI Safety & Ethics.\n\n**Key Algorithms & Models**\n- Classical: Linear/Logistic regression, decision trees, SVMs, k‑NN.\n- Neural: Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs), Recurrent Neural Networks/LSTMs, Transformers (attention‑based).\n- Reinforcement Learning: Q‑learning, policy gradients, Deep Q‑Networks (DQNs).\n- Probabilistic: Bayesian networks, Markov Decision Processes.\n- Generative: GANs, VAEs, diffusion models.\n\n**Major Applications**\n- Healthcare: diagnosis, drug discovery, personalized treatment.\n- Finance: fraud detection, algorithmic trading, credit scoring.\n- Transportation: autonomous vehicles, traffic optimization.\n- Customer Service: chatbots, sentiment analysis, recommendation systems.\n- Manufacturing: predictive maintenance, quality inspection, supply‑chain optimization.\n- Science: protein folding (AlphaFold), climate modeling, materials discovery.\n\n**Ethical, Legal & Societal Concerns**\n- Bias and discrimination from training data.\n- Transparency & explainability of “black‑box” models.\n- Data privacy and large‑scale data scraping.\n- Job displacement vs. augmentation.\n- Dual‑use risks (disinformation, deepfakes, autonomous weapons).\n- Emerging regulations: EU AI Act, US executive orders, ISO/IEC AI standards.\n\n**Performance Benchmarks**\n- ImageNet: state‑of‑the‑art top‑1 accuracy ~88% (vs. 57% in 2012).\n- GLUE / SuperGLUE: language understanding; GPT‑4 >\u202f90%.\n- Atari 2600: human‑level performance with DQN.\n- AlphaGo/AlphaZero: superhuman play in Go, chess, shogi.\n\n**Current Research Frontiers**\n- Foundation models: scaling laws, emergent abilities, multimodal integration.\n- Efficient AI: model compression, sparsity, neuromorphic hardware.\n- Robustness: adversarial defenses, out‑of‑distribution detection.\n- Alignment & safety: value learning, corrigibility, safe exploration.\n- Neurosymbolic AI: blending neural perception with symbolic reasoning.\n- Continual / lifelong learning: mitigating catastrophic forgetting.\n\n**Future Outlook (2025‑2035)**\n- Proliferation of domain‑specific foundation models (legal, medical, etc.).\n- Stronger regulatory frameworks guiding development and deployment.\n- Advances toward general‑purpose AI agents capable of cross‑modal planning.\n- Greater emphasis on energy‑efficient AI to reduce carbon footprints.\n- AI‑augmented scientific discovery accelerating breakthroughs in medicine, materials, and climate solutions.\n\nFeel free to let me know if you need a deeper dive into any of these topics.\n\nBest regards,\nAI Research Assistant', 'subject': 'Summary of Artificial Intelligence Research', 'to': 'me@example.com'})
